# ── Derived data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything under data/ is reproducible: calibrated/ re-downloads from MAST, and
# drizzled/ + drizzle_files/ regenerate from the scripts. Provenance lives in the
# info/*.json tracking files (which obsids produced which product), not in the bytes.
# ~185 GB across ~3900 FITS files, so it must never enter git history.
#
# data/cutouts is the deliberate exception: the final science stamps (12" square, the
# pipeline default -- see scripts/cutout_paths.py) are small (~500 MB) and worth
# versioning across pipeline changes; it also carries scripts/make_masks.py's hand-drawn
# GUI masks (cutout_[cr_]mask.fits), which are NOT regenerable by any script, so losing
# them means redoing manual mask work. data/mosaics is the same deal: small QC grids
# generated from the cutouts by scripts/make_mosaics.py. The *_<size>arcsec/ size
# variants (e.g. data/cutouts_20arcsec/, the old default) are NOT versioned: they are
# regenerable from the same drizzled mosaics by one runner call (run_cutouts_all.sh
# <sample> <size>), and carry no masks of their own since make_masks.py targets the
# default (12") tree.
#
# There is ONE stamp per (sample, lens, filter) in there (2026-09-14): the bad-column-filled
# reduction (--bcfill) supersedes the standard one in place for the ACS/WFPC2 bands it
# covers, rather than in the parallel data/cutouts_bcfill/ + data/mosaics_bcfill/ trees it
# used to occupy. Which reduction a stamp is comes from its BCFILL header card and the
# matching `bcfill` key in info/lens_cutout_qc.json, not from its path. The drizzle layer
# still has both (data/drizzled[_bcfill]/, data/drizzle_files[_bcfill]/) and all of it stays
# ignored by the data/* rule.
data/*
!data/cutouts/
!data/mosaics/
# ── Positions QC overlays ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/make_positions.py writes TWO files per band: cutout_[cr_]positions.json, the
# hand-marked image positions themselves -- non-regenerable manual work, tracked like the
# masks -- and cutout_[cr_]positions.png, a QC view OF that JSON. Only the JSON is a
# product. The PNG is one per band (~160 of them) and is rebuilt from the JSON + the sci
# stamp with no GUI and no re-clicking:
#     uv run python scripts/make_positions.py --sample <sample> --overlays-only
# so it is regenerable in the sense this file cares about, and stays out of history.
# NOTE this is the one PNG under data/cutouts/ that is ignored -- cutout_cr.png,
# _dataset.png and _mask_arcs.png are all still tracked.
data/cutouts/**/*_positions.png

# ── slacs_gold f606W arc masks: parked, not abandoned (2026-09-21) ─────────────
# The slacs_gold f814W arc masks (38/38) are committed; its f606W ones (10 so far) are
# held OUT of git for now at the user's request. Nothing is deleted: the .fits and .png
# stay on disk beside the sci they were drawn on and their provenance stays in
# info/lens_arc_masks.json, so make_arc_masks.py still counts them done and skips them
# (--force to redraw). Drop these two lines to commit them.
# NOTE this is the ONLY _mask_arcs file under data/cutouts/ that is ignored -- gallery's
# and slacs_other's f606W arc masks, and slacs_gold's own f814W ones, are all tracked.
data/cutouts/slacs_gold/*/f606W/cutout_cr_mask_arcs.fits
data/cutouts/slacs_gold/*/f606W/cutout_cr_mask_arcs.png

# ...and neither is the per-size QC provenance for an untracked size, which would
# otherwise be a tracked file describing products nobody else has on disk. The default
# (12") info/lens_cutout_qc.json is tracked as an ordinary info/ file, untouched by this
# pattern.
info/lens_cutout_qc_*arcsec.json

# ── Large external material ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# info/data_handbooks is intentionally NOT ignored: the instrument handbooks are the
# cited source for the DQ-bit and pixel-scale choices, so they travel with the repo.
hst_notebooks/

# ── Superseded notebooks ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Exploratory / pre-pipeline notebooks. Kept locally but not versioned: they carry
# large embedded output images and re-run churn (execution counts, timestamps) that
# does not belong in history. The live pipeline is scripts/*.py.
scripts/old_notebooks/

# ── Generated output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
output/

# ── Editor / agent / interpreter state ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Track shared Claude Code config (.claude/settings.json) but keep personal
# per-machine overrides (settings.local.json) out of history.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store

# ── uv-managed environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# pyproject.toml/uv.lock/.python-version are tracked (they define the env, including
# the exact CPython build); the venv itself is machine-local and rebuilt via `uv sync`.
.venv/

# ── SLACS SNAP F814W test recoveries (2026-09-14) ──────────────────────────────
# Three slacs_other lenses had their ACS F814W drizzled past the 500s BLOCK_EXPTIME gate
# (drizzle_acs_wfc.py --block-exptime 400) purely to attempt cross-band COLOUR tests while
# judging masks. They are single 420s SLACS snapshot frames: no dither, no frame-to-frame
# CR rejection, CR holes that can land on the target, and depth ~10x below the F606W they
# were compared against -- on J1538+5817 the test failed outright (a ring image measured
# S/N -17.7, i.e. model error). They are diagnostics, not science products, so the pixels
# stay out of git while remaining on disk for further tests. The tracking JSONs are kept at
# their gated values (f814W null) to match: the science inventory should not list a product
# the repo does not carry. Re-create with the --block-exptime flag; see AGENTS.md.
data/cutouts/slacs_other/J1134+6027/f814W/
data/cutouts/slacs_other/J1403+0006/f814W/
data/cutouts/slacs_other/J1538+5817/f814W/

# ── diagnostics/ ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One-off QC and investigation figures (LACosmic scans, arc-vs-contaminant tests, mask
# proposals). They are regenerable from the scripts and the products in data/, they are
# read once while judging a decision, and they accumulate fast, so they stay out of git.
# The DECISION each figure supported belongs in AGENTS.md / info/*.json, which is where a
# reader should find it -- so do not cite a diagnostics/ path as evidence in a commit
# message or a note without also stating the numbers, because a fresh clone will not have
# the image. Untracked from 2026-09-14; the five previously-committed PNGs remain in git
# history.
diagnostics/
